    {
      "title": "Value creation",
      "paragraphs": [
        "Organic growth is the primary engine of value creation. The base case underwrites 22% annual EBITDA growth, reflecting CrowdStrike's continued module adoption across its Falcon platform, expanding wallet share within existing enterprise accounts, and new logo generation driven by increasing regulatory and threat-landscape pressure on security budgets. This growth rate is defensible given CRWD's demonstrated land-and-expand motion and the structural shift toward consolidated security platforms displacing point solutions.",
        "Margin expansion compounds the organic growth story. A 70% free cash flow conversion rate reflects the high incremental margins inherent in a cloud-native SaaS model with largely fixed infrastructure costs and a predominantly subscription-based revenue mix. As revenue scales, S&M efficiency improves and R&D is increasingly amortized across a larger base, driving EBITDA margin progression that supports the FCF conversion assumption.",
        "Multiple expansion provides an additional layer of return. The thesis underwrites an exit at 20.0x EBITDA versus an entry multiple of 18.0x \u2014 a 2-turn expansion that is conservative relative to peer precedents for high-growth cybersecurity platforms. The capital structure is financed at 5.0x debt/EBITDA, a leverage level that preserves operational flexibility while meaningfully amplifying equity returns. Total exit equity value reaches $32.4B, implying a full sponsor return on the $7.8B equity commitment."
      ],
